    <briefdescription>
<para>Broadcast task. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Besides usual task fields, stores a list of interfaces available for broadcast packets. The task works asynchronously just like its ancestor, because even broadcast packets can not be sent without explicit permission from libev in a form of EV_WRITE event.</para><para>Despite usually having multiple network interfaces supporting broadcast, there is only one task to send a packet to all of them. The same task works multiple times, each time sending a packet to one interface. After completion it is self-deleted. There are no any concrete reason behind that except stint on memory for multiple tasks. </para>    </detaileddescription>
